          "type": "user",
          "text": "     1→# File Upload Feature Plan\n     2→\n     3→## Overview\n     4→\n     5→Add file attachment support to the chat UI, allowing users to drag-and-drop or select files to send alongside messages to the AI.\n     6→\n     7→## Requirements\n     8→\n     9→- User can drag-and-drop or click to add files to the chat input\n    10→- Files display as chips with an \"x\" button to remove\n    11→- Files remain as local `File` references until send\n    12→- \"Upload\" (S3 or base64 conversion) happens only at send time\n    13→- Only lightweight file metadata (name, size, type) is persisted - not file data\n    14→- When loading persisted messages, unavailable files show a placeholder\n    15→- Abstract `FileUploadBackend` interface for future S3 support\n    16→- Configurable max file size (default 10MB)\n    17→\n    18→## AG-UI Protocol Compatibility\n    19→\n    20→AG-UI supports multimodal content in user messages:\n    21→\n    22→```typescript\n    23→interface UserMessage {\n    24→  id: string;\n    25→  role: \"user\";\n    26→  content: string | MultimodalContent[];\n    27→}\n    28→\n    29→interface MultimodalContent {\n    30→  type: \"text\" | \"image\" | \"audio\" | \"file\";\n    31→  // Type-specific fields\n    32→}\n    33→```\n    34→\n    35→## Architecture\n    36→\n    37→### Type Definitions\n    38→\n    39→#### File Upload Types (`packages/client/src/fileUpload/types.ts`)\n    40→\n    41→```typescript\n    42→export const DEFAULT_MAX_FILE_SIZE = 10 * 1024 * 1024; // 10MB\n    43→\n    44→/** Persisted file metadata (lightweight, for storage) */\n    45→export interface PersistedFileMetadata {\n    46→  name: string;\n    47→  size: number;\n    48→  mimeType: string;\n    49→}\n    50→\n    51→/** Runtime file attachment (local File reference until send) */\n    52→export interface FileAttachment {\n    53→  id: string;\n    54→  file: File;\n    55→  preview?: string;  // data URL for image thumbnails (generated on attach)\n    56→}\n    57→\n    58→/** Abstract file upload backend - converts File to URL at send time */\n    59→export interface FileUploadBackend {\n    60→  /**\n    61→   * Prepare file for sending to AI.\n    62→   * Called at send time - converts File to URL.\n    63→   * For embed: converts to base64 data URL\n    64→   * For S3: uploads and returns public URL\n    65→   */\n    66→  prepareForSend(file: File): Promise<string>;\n    67→}\n    68→\n    69→/** Configuration for file uploads */\n    70→export interface FileUploadConfig {\n    71→  /** Backend for converting files to URLs at send time */\n    72→  backend?: FileUploadBackend;\n    73→  /** Max file size in bytes (default: 10MB) */\n    74→  maxFileSize?: number;\n    75→  /** Accepted MIME types (undefined = all) */\n    76→  acceptedTypes?: string[];\n    77→}\n    78→```\n    79→\n    80→#### Multimodal Content Types (`packages/core/src/types.ts`)\n    81→\n    82→```typescript\n    83→/** Content part for multimodal messages */\n    84→export type MultimodalContent =\n    85→  | { type: 'text'; text: string }\n    86→  | { type: 'image'; url: string }\n    87→  | { type: 'file'; url: string; mimeType: string; name: string };\n    88→\n    89→/** User message content - string or multimodal */\n    90→export type UserMessageContent = string | MultimodalContent[];\n    91→```\n    92→\n    93→#### Persistence Types (`packages/client/src/providers/chatRepository/types.ts`)\n    94→\n    95→```typescript\n    96→/** Content part for persisted messages */\n    97→export type PersistedContentPart =\n    98→  | { type: 'text'; text: string }\n    99→  | { type: 'file'; file: PersistedFileMetadata };\n   100→\n   101→/** Content that can be persisted */\n   102→export type PersistedMessageContent = string | PersistedContentPart[];\n   103→\n   104→export interface PersistedMessage {\n   105→  id: string;\n   106→  role: 'user' | 'assistant' | 'tool';\n   107→  content: PersistedMessageContent;  // Updated from just string\n   108→  createdAt: Date;\n   109→  displayMode?: MessageDisplayMode;\n   110→}\n   111→```\n   112→\n   113→### Backend Implementations\n   114→\n   115→#### EmbedFileUploadBackend (`packages/client/src/fileUpload/EmbedFileUploadBackend.ts`)\n   116→\n   117→Single-method implementation - converts File to base64 data URL:\n   118→\n   119→```typescript\n   120→export class EmbedFileUploadBackend implements FileUploadBackend {\n   121→  async prepareForSend(file: File): Promise<string> {\n   122→    return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\n   123→      const reader = new FileReader();\n   124→      reader.onload = () => resolve(reader.result as string);\n   125→      reader.onerror = () => reject(new Error('Failed to read file'));\n   126→      reader.readAsDataURL(file);\n   127→    });\n   128→  }\n   129→}\n   130→```\n   131→\n   132→#### Future: S3FileUploadBackend\n   133→\n   134→```typescript\n   135→export class S3FileUploadBackend implements FileUploadBackend {\n   136→  constructor(private getPresignedUrl: (file: File) => Promise<{ uploadUrl: string; publicUrl: string }>) {}\n   137→\n   138→  async prepareForSend(file: File): Promise<string> {\n   139→    const { uploadUrl, publicUrl } = await this.getPresignedUrl(file);\n   140→    await this.uploadToS3(uploadUrl, file);\n   141→    return publicUrl;\n   142→  }\n   143→}\n   144→```\n   145→\n   146→### UI Components\n   147→\n   148→#### FileChip (`packages/client/src/components/FileChip.tsx`)\n   149→\n   150→Small chip component showing:\n   151→- Thumbnail (for images)\n   152→- File name (truncated)\n   153→- Remove button (×)\n   154→\n   155→```typescript\n   156→interface FileChipProps {\n   157→  attachment: FileAttachment;\n   158→  onRemove: () => void;\n   159→}\n   160→```\n   161→\n   162→#### UseAIChatPanel Updates\n   163→\n   164→- Add `fileUploadConfig` prop\n   165→- Add drag-and-drop zone (entire input area)\n   166→- Add \"+\" button next to input for file picker (hidden `<input type=\"file\">`)\n   167→- Render file chips above the text input\n   168→- Handle file validation (size, type)\n   169→- Update `onSendMessage` signature to include attachments\n   170→\n   171→### Data Flow\n   172→\n   173→```\n   174→1. User drops file(s) OR clicks \"+\" button and selects file(s)\n   175→   → Validate size against config.maxFileSize\n   176→   → Create FileAttachment with File object (local reference)\n   177→   → Generate preview for images (small data URL for thumbnail only)\n   178→   → Display as chip\n   179→\n   180→2. User clicks Send\n   181→   → For each attachment: backend.prepareForSend(file) → URL\n   182→   → Build MultimodalContent[] for AI (with URLs)\n   183→   → Build PersistedContentPart[] for storage (metadata only: name, size, mimeType)\n   184→   → Send to AI via client.sendPrompt()\n   185→   → Save to ChatRepository (metadata only)\n   186→\n   187→3. Loading persisted message with file metadata\n   188→   → Show placeholder: \"[📎 filename - no longer available]\"\n   189→   → (Future S3: could store URL in metadata and display)\n   190→```\n   191→\n   192→## Implementation Steps\n   193→\n   194→### Phase 1: Core Types and Backend\n   195→\n   196→1. Create `packages/client/src/fileUpload/types.ts`\n   197→   - Export `DEFAULT_MAX_FILE_SIZE`, `PersistedFileMetadata`, `FileAttachment`, `FileUploadBackend`, `FileUploadConfig`\n   198→\n   199→2. Create `packages/client/src/fileUpload/EmbedFileUploadBackend.ts`\n   200→   - Single method: `prepareForSend(file: File): Promise<string>`\n   201→\n   202→3. Create `packages/client/src/fileUpload/index.ts`\n   203→   - Re-export all types and classes\n   204→\n   205→4. Update `packages/core/src/types.ts`\n   206→   - Add `MultimodalContent` type\n   207→   - Add `UserMessageContent` type\n   208→\n   209→### Phase 2: Persistence Layer\n   210→\n   211→5. Update `packages/client/src/providers/chatRepository/types.ts`\n   212→   - Import `PersistedFileMetada